{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobsearch.illinoisstate.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-professor-tenure-track-in-actuarial-science-normal-illinois-illinois-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor (Tenure Track) in Actuarial Science",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor (Tenure Track) in Actuarial Science - Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States Home Job Postings Applicant Accomodations Community My Profile Kiosk mode Job Description Assistant/Associate Professor (Tenure Track) in Actuarial Science Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States On Campus Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant/Associate Professor (Tenure Track) in Actuarial Science Division Name: Academic Affairs College/Unit: College of Arts and Sciences Department: Mathematics Campus Location: Normal, IL Job Summary The Department of Mathematics as a part of the College of Arts and Sciences at Illinois State University in Normal, IL invites applications for a nine-month tenure-track position in Actuarial Science at the level of Assistant/Associate Professor. Successful candidates are expected to work with the Actuarial Program in the administration and service areas, teach courses related to actuarial science, pursue research and professional involvement in actuarial science, and otherwise contribute to the life of the department. Refereed research publications, quality teaching, and professional service are required for tenure. University Benefit Highlights: - Insurance benefits, including health, dental, vision, and life - Retirement and supplemental retirement planning options - Tuition waiver benefits available to staff as well as their eligible dependents - Paid holiday/administrative closures during Thanksgiving and Winter Breaks - Paid benefit time Additional University Benefit information, including information regarding eligibility to participate in the State Universities Retirement System and the State of Illinois Group Insurance program, can be reviewed here: https://hr.illinoisstate.edu/benefits/ Additional Information The Mathematics Department offers Bachelor’s and Master’s degrees in mathematics, and a Ph.D. degree in mathematics education. Within the Bachelor’s program there are sequences in mathematics, mathematics education, statistics, actuarial science. The Master’s program offers specializations in mathematics, statistics, actuarial science (also available online), biomathematics, and mathematics education (online). Consult our web site at www.math.ilstu.edu for more information. Illinois State University is a Center of Actuarial Excellence (CAE) with University Earned Credit (see https://www.soa.org/education/resources/cae/default ), and was awarded the CAE recognition in December 2009, among the first nine universities in the United States, and the first in the state of Illinois. Illinois State University is also a Gold Level Partner in the University Recognition Program of Casualty Actuarial Society and won two Casualty Actuarial Society University Awards. Illinois State University is also a Global Center of Insurance Excellence. Founded in 1857 as Illinois’ first public university, Illinois State University, IllinoisState.edu is one of only 27 institutions nationwide to earn both Research 2 (R2) and Opportunity Colleges and Universities (OCU) designations by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education, which recognizes campuses that foster student success and research. We enroll approximately 21,000 students in six colleges. Our new strategic plan, Excellence by Design: 2024-2029, lists our seven core values: Excellence in Teaching, Learning, and Scholarship; Individualized Attention; Equity, Diversity, Access, and Belonging; Collaboration; Community and Civic Engagement; Respect; and Integrity. By acting on these values, we create a learning environment that results in our university being the first-choice public university in Illinois for high-achieving, motivated students who seek an individualized educational experience combined with the resources of a large university. Learn more about Illinois State’s Metrics of Excellence at IllinoisState.edu/PointsofPride . Bloomington-Normal: Illinois State University is located in the growing twin cities of Bloomington and Normal, with a metro population of approximately 172,000. The community is also home to Illinois Wesleyan University, Heartland Community College, St. Joseph Medical Center, Carle BroMenn Medical Center, COUNTRY Financial, State Farm Insurance’s International Headquarters, Central Illinois Regional Airport, and electric truck manufacturer Rivian Motors. The community has distinguished itself for its outstanding school systems, and its citizens’ high level of educational attainment, as well as its parks and recreation, health care, vibrant fine arts scene, job growth, economic opportunity, historic sites, and low crime rates. Bloomington made Livability’s top 100 Best Places to Live (2024) and ranked No. 3 on College Values Online’s list of Best Small College Towns in America (2024). Bloomington-Normal is conveniently located about three hours from Indianapolis; two hours from both Chicago and St. Louis; and an hour from Peoria, Champaign-Urbana, Decatur, and Springfield. Many of these locations are accessible from Bloomington-Normal via Amtrak, which is located one block from Illinois State’s campus. For more information on our community, visit visitbn.org . Salary Rate / Pay Rate Salary is $72,828-$108,000,commensurate with qualifications and experience. Required Qualifications A Ph.D. in Mathematics, Actuarial Science, Statistics, or an Actuarial- Science-related area Possession of a professional actuarial credential, or dedicated pursuit of one State law mandates demonstrable oral proficiency in the English language as a requirement of this position. Work Hours Varies Proposed Starting Date August 16, 2027 Required Applicant Documents Current CV Short (2-3 pages) description of your research experience and planned future research Short (2-3 pages) description outlining your teaching experience Contact information for 3 references Please Note : These documents are required to be submitted online in order to complete the application process. Please have these documents ready prior to clicking on \"Apply\" Special Instructions for Applicants The review of applications will begin on November 12, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. All work under this appointment is required to be performed from within the State of Illinois. Illinois State University does not authorize out-of-state work. Contact Information for Applicants Questions about the search should be directed to Cassandra Snelling (clsnell1@ilstu.edu). Important Information for Applicants This position is subject to a criminal background investigation and if applicable, an employment history review, based on University Policy 3.1.30 and any offer of employment is contingent upon you passing a satisfactory criminal background investigation and/or an employment history review. You may not begin work until the criminal background investigation results have been received and cleared by Human Resources. Illinois State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran. If you are an individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) or other state or federal law you may request an accommodation by contacting the Office of Equal Opportunity and Access at (309) 438-3383 . The Office of Equal Opportunity and Access will hold any confidential information you provide in confidence. If you are having difficulty accessing the system, please call Human Resources at (309) 438-8311 . Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 4abca40b Last Name (required) 642a9451 Email (required) c6aad360 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 135b40f2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type On Campus On Campus Locations Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States First Name (required) 25af2752 Last Name (required) e7f86b50 Email (required) 63f5fa48 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Illinois State University, Normal, IL USA Cookie Preferences Privacy Statement Appropriate Use Policy Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://jobsearch.illinoisstate.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-scenic-design-normal-illinois-illinois-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Scenic Design",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Scenic Design - Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States Home Job Postings Applicant Accomodations Community My Profile Kiosk mode Job Description Assistant Professor of Scenic Design Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States On Campus Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant Professor of Scenic Design Employee Classification: Asst Professor Division Name: Academic Affairs College/Unit: Wonsook Kim College of Fine Arts Department: School of Theatre, Dance, and Film Campus Location: Normal, IL Job Summary The School of Theatre, Dance, and Film invites applications for a tenure-track position to lead its Scenic Design program, which includes the MFA in Scenic Design. This position will teach, mentor, and recruit undergraduate and graduate students. Responsibilities include scholarly research and/or creative activity, effective undergraduate and graduate teaching, and service. The successful candidate will teach scenic design and related areas of contemporary production design for live performance but may also include other professional interests such as production design for film and media, projection and media design, and other innovative approaches to visual storytelling. The normal teaching load is nine credit hours (3 courses) per semester and mentorship of undergraduate and graduate students. Occasional designing during the School’s season may also be available. The School of Theatre, Dance, and Film and Wonsook Kim College of Fine Arts are committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, belonging, and academic excellence in teaching, research/creative activity, and service. We value the contributions of faculty who support student success and cultivate collaborative learning environments that encourage curiosity, creativity, and professional growth. Candidates should demonstrate a commitment to student-centered teaching and mentoring practices that engage and support students with diverse experiences, perspectives, and educational goals. Successful applicants will be prepared to mentor undergraduate and graduate students, promote student-driven artistic and scholarly inquiry, and contribute to a culture of collaboration within the School, College, and broader professional community. We seek a colleague who values partnership, interdisciplinary engagement, and shared governance in advancing the mission of the School and University. ISU is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes applications from qualified candidates. Illinois State University Benefits Highlights: - Insurance benefits, including health, dental, vision, and life - Retirement and supplemental retirement planning options - Tuition waiver benefits available to staff as well as their eligible dependents - Paid holidays and administrative closures during Thanksgiving and Winter Break - Paid benefit time (e.g., personal plus time and sick time) Additional University Benefit information, including information regarding eligibility to participate in the State Universities Retirement System and the State of Illinois Group Insurance program, can be reviewed here: https://hr.illinoisstate.edu/benefits/ Additional Information The School of Theatre, Dance, and Film is one of four schools within the Wonsook Kim College of Fine Arts. The School has nearly 400 undergraduate and graduate students enrolled in its programs, which include B.A./B.S.programs in Acting, Dance, Dance Teacher Education, Film, Musical Theatre, Production Design and Technology, Theatre Studies and Theatre Teacher Education; M.A./M.S. in Theatre Studies, and M.F.A. in Directing and Design (Costume, Lighting, and Scenic Design). Its current season consist of 6-8 theatre and dance productions in two facilities, a 525-seat proscenium space and a flexible space that can be adapted to a 125-seat thrust or 150-seat arena. The School is home to the Illinois Shakespeare Festival and maintains membership in URTA and accreditation by NAST. See https:/finearts.illinoisstate.edu/theatre-dance/ Illinois State University, IllinoisState.edu , was founded in 1857 as Illinois’ first public university. We enroll approximately 21,000 students in six colleges. Our new strategic plan, Excellence by Design: 2024-2029, lists our seven core values: Excellence in Teaching, Learning, and Scholarship; Individualized Attention; Equity, Diversity, Access, and Belonging; Collaboration; Community and Civic Engagement; Respect; and Integrity. By acting on these values, we create a learning environment that results in our university being the first-choice public university in Illinois for high-achieving, motivated students who seek an individualized educational experience combined with the resources of a large university. Learn more about Illinois State’s Metrics of Excellence at IllinoisState.edu/PointsofPride . Bloomington-Normal: Illinois State University is located in the growing twin cities of Bloomington and Normal, with a metro population of approximately 172,000. The community is also home to Illinois Wesleyan University, Heartland Community College, St. Joseph Medical Center, Carle BroMenn Medical Center, COUNTRY Financial, State Farm Insurance’s International Headquarters, Central Illinois Regional Airport, and electric truck manufacturer Rivian Motors. The community has distinguished itself for its outstanding school systems, and its citizens’ high level of educational attainment, as well as its parks and recreation, health care, vibrant fine arts scene, job growth, economic opportunity, historic sites, and low crime rates. Bloomington made Livability’s top 100 Best Places to Live (2024) and ranked No. 3 on College Values Online’s list of Best Small College Towns in America (2024). Bloomington-Normal is conveniently located about three hours from Indianapolis; two hours from both Chicago and St. Louis; and an hour from Peoria, Champaign-Urbana, Decatur, and Springfield. Many of these locations are accessible from Bloomington-Normal via Amtrak, which is located one block from Illinois State’s campus. For more information on our community, visit visitbn.org . Salary Rate / Pay Rate $72,828-$74,285 Required Qualifications 1) Hold an M.F.A. or another terminal degree with a focus in Scenic Design or a related field. 2) Have demonstrated professional experience in scenic design at the regional, national and/or international levels. 3) Have demonstrated ability to teach, mentor, and support students from a wide range of backgrounds and experiences; evidence of effective collaboration with colleagues, students, and community partners; and a commitment to creating an inclusive and supportive learning environment. 4) Be able to demonstrate oral proficiency in the English language as a requirement for this position as mandated by state law. Work Hours Varies Proposed Starting Date August 16, 2027 Required Applicant Documents 1) Letter of application 2) Portfolio 3) Curriculum Vitae 4) 2-3 page statement of teaching philosophy 5) Names and contact information for three professional references Please Note : These documents are required to be submitted online in order to complete the application process. Please have these documents ready prior to clicking on \"Apply\" Special Instructions for Applicants Review of applications will begin November 9, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Contact Information for Applicants Natasha Warloe nmwarlo@ilstu.edu 309-438-8785 Important Information for Applicants This position is subject to a criminal background investigation and if applicable, an employment history review, based on University Policy 3.1.30 and any offer of employment is contingent upon you passing a satisfactory criminal background investigation and/or an employment history review. You may not begin work until the criminal background investigation results have been received and cleared by Human Resources. Illinois State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran. If you are an individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) or other state or federal law you may request an accommodation by contacting the Office of Equal Opportunity and Access at (309) 438-3383 . The Office of Equal Opportunity and Access will hold any confidential information you provide in confidence. If you are having difficulty accessing the system, please call Human Resources at (309) 438-8311 . Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) f8a9c0eb Last Name (required) 86dd5a63 Email (required) 6f9375d9 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 2ebcf347 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type On Campus On Campus Locations Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States First Name (required) 587502ce Last Name (required) 98d8f00d Email (required) 03912b91 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Illinois State University, Normal, IL USA Cookie Preferences Privacy Statement Appropriate Use Policy Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
