    "https://jobsearch.illinoisstate.edu/jobs/instructional-assistant-professor-non-tenure-track-faculty-mcn-normal-illinois-illinois-united-states-3d87c5ae-e9bf-447f-adef-88a57632f2c3": {
      "title": "Instructional Assistant Professor - Non-Tenure Track Faculty - MCN",
      "description": "Instructional Assistant Professor - Non-Tenure Track Faculty - MCN - Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States Home Job Postings Applicant Accomodations Community My Profile Kiosk mode Job Description Instructional Assistant Professor - Non-Tenure Track Faculty - MCN Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States On Campus Add to favorites View favorites Title: Instructional Assistant Professor - Non-Tenure Track Faculty - MCN Employee Classification: Instructional Asst Professor Division Name: Academic Affairs College/Unit: Mennonite College of Nursing Department: Mennonite College of Nursing Campus Location: Normal, IL Job Summary For over 100 years, Mennonite College of Nursing (MCN) has had a reputation for innovation and excellence. As the only professional college at Illinois State University, we offer traditional and online programs, including prelicensure, RN to BSN, and accelerated baccalaureate degrees; an MSN program with Family Nurse Practitioner and Nursing Leadership Management sequences, a Ph.D. in nursing science, and a Doctor of Nursing Practice program. As a leader in research on aging/vulnerable populations, heart failure, and nursing education science, MCN is an excellent environment for candidates to share their clinical and teaching expertise. The Mennonite College of Nursing at Illinois State University invites qualified individuals to apply for a nine month, full-time, non-tenure track appointment to teach in-person classes, as an Instructional Assistant Professor. The individual selected will be expected to teach 24 credit-hour equivalents of courses per Academic Year. Teaching assignments may be at either Mennonite College of Nursing location – Normal or Springfield – or any of our clinicals sites, which may be up to a one-hour drive from Normal. University Benefit Highlights: - Insurance benefits, including health, dental, vision, and life (eligibility determination) - Retirement and supplemental retirement planning options - Tuition waiver benefits available to staff as well as their eligible dependents - Paid benefit time Additional University Benefit information, including information regarding eligibility to participate in the State Universities Retirement System and the State of Illinois Group Insurance program, can be reviewed here: https://hr.illinoisstate.edu/benefits/ Additional Information For more information about Mennonite College of Nursing, please visit our website at http://nursing.illinoisstate.edu/ Illinois State University: Illinois State University, IllinoisState.edu, was founded in 1857 as Illinois’ first public university. We enroll approximately 21,000 students in six colleges. Our new strategic plan, Excellence by Design: 2024-2029, lists our seven core values: Excellence in Teaching, Learning, and Scholarship; Individualized Attention; Equity, Diversity, Access, and Belonging; Collaboration; Community and Civic Engagement; Respect; and Integrity. By acting on these values, we create a learning environment that results in our university being the first-choice public university in Illinois for high-achieving, motivated students who seek an individualized educational experience combined with the resources of a large university. Learn more about Illinois State’s Metrics of Excellence at IllinoisState.edu/PointsofPride . Bloomington-Normal: Illinois State University is located in the growing twin cities of Bloomington and Normal, with a metro population of approximately 172,000. The community is also home to Illinois Wesleyan University, Heartland Community College, St. Joseph Medical Center, Carle BroMenn Medical Center, COUNTRY Financial, State Farm Insurance’s International Headquarters, Central Illinois Regional Airport, and electric truck manufacturer Rivian Motors. The community has distinguished itself for its outstanding school systems, and its citizens’ high level of educational attainment, as well as its parks and recreation, health care, vibrant fine arts scene, job growth, economic opportunity, historic sites, and low crime rates. Bloomington made Livability’s top 100 Best Places to Live (2024) and ranked No. 3 on College Values Online’s list of Best Small College Towns in America (2024). Bloomington-Normal is conveniently located about three hours from Indianapolis; two hours from both Chicago and St. Louis; and an hour from Peoria, Champaign-Urbana, Decatur, and Springfield. Many of these locations are accessible from Bloomington-Normal via Amtrak, which is located one block from Illinois State’s campus. For more information on our community, visit visitbn.org . Salary Rate / Pay Rate $70,000-$75,000 per 9 month Academic Year Required Qualifications Masters of Science in Nursing completed by the start date of the appointment. Passion for teaching undergraduate students in the clinical, laboratory and classroom setting. Must have licensure in Illinois by the start date of the appointment. For teaching positions, state law mandates demonstrable oral proficiency in the English language as a requirement for this position. Preferred Qualifications Doctor of Nursing Practice completed by the start date of the appointment. Previous teaching experience in a clinical, laboratory and/or classroom setting Experience in maternal/infant nursing, psych mental health, acute care, critical care, pediatrics and/or public health APRN licensure, preferably FNP or PMHNP Work Hours Varies Proposed Starting Date January 1, 2027 Required Applicant Documents Cover Letter Resume/CV Reference List Please Note : These documents are required to be submitted online in order to complete the application process. Please have these documents ready prior to clicking on \"Apply\" Special Instructions for Applicants All work under this appointment is required to be performed from within the State of Illinois. Applicants for this position must be authorized to work in the U.S. without ISU sponsorship. Sponsorship for work authorization will not be considered for this position. Contact Information for Applicants Lissa Bevins at mabevin@ilstu.edu Important Information for Applicants This position is subject to a criminal background investigation and if applicable, an employment history review, based on University Policy 3.1.30 and any offer of employment is contingent upon you passing a satisfactory criminal background investigation and/or an employment history review. You may not begin work until the criminal background investigation results have been received and cleared by Human Resources. Illinois State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran. If you are an individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) or other state or federal law you may request an accommodation by contacting the Office of Equal Opportunity and Access at (309) 438-3383 . The Office of Equal Opportunity and Access will hold any confidential information you provide in confidence. If you are having difficulty accessing the system, please call Human Resources at (309) 438-8311 . Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 0a812a3e Last Name (required) 19c61b55 Email (required) d1e75e28 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign up for job alerts Job Alert eaa850b0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type On Campus On Campus Locations Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States First Name (required) 46f37f84 Last Name (required) aeda839a Email (required) 525fbbdf Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Illinois State University, Normal, IL USA Cookie Preferences Privacy Statement Appropriate Use Policy Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
