    "https://jobsearch.illinoisstate.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-in-environmental-geochemistry-normal-illinois-illinois-united-states": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR IN ENVIRONMENTAL GEOCHEMISTRY",
      "description": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR IN ENVIRONMENTAL GEOCHEMISTRY - Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States Home Job Postings Applicant Accomodations Community My Profile Kiosk mode Job Description ASSISTANT PROFESSOR IN ENVIRONMENTAL GEOCHEMISTRY Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States On Campus Add to favorites View favorites Title: ASSISTANT PROFESSOR IN ENVIRONMENTAL GEOCHEMISTRY Employee Classification: Asst Professor Division Name: Academic Affairs College/Unit: College of Arts and Sciences Department: Geography, Geology, and the Environment Campus Location: Normal, IL Job Summary The Department of Geography, Geology, and the Environment (GEO) ( https://geo.illinoisstate.edu/ ) at Illinois State University seeks an environmental geochemist with an emphasis in water resources to help lead our growth as we expand programs in hydrogeology and environmental science. We invite applications for a nine-month, tenure-track position in Environmental Geochemistry at the Assistant Professor level. The successful candidate is expected to demonstrate a commitment to maintaining and growing meaningful research collaborations and externally funded research. This commitment should be reflected in the research agenda and the application materials. Primary teaching responsibilities will include a combination of existing and new courses in the candidate’s area of expertise at the introductory, upper-, and graduate levels. Teaching aqueous geochemistry is a required part of the position; the teaching load will also include other courses that could include a relevant introductory/General Education course, environmental geology, or upper-/graduate-level environmental or water courses. An expectation of this position, which is at the intersection of Geology, Hydrogeology, and Environmental Science, is attracting new students into our existing undergraduate major programs and recruiting and advising students in the Hydrogeology M.S. program. University Benefit Highlights: - Insurance benefits, including health, dental, vision, and life - Retirement and supplemental retirement planning options - Tuition waiver benefits available to staff as well as their eligible dependents - Paid holiday/administrative closures during Thanksgiving and Winter Breaks - Paid benefit time Additional University Benefit information, including information regarding eligibility to participate in the State Universities Retirement System and the State of Illinois Group Insurance program, can be reviewed here: https://hr.illinoisstate.edu/benefits/ Additional Information Founded in 1857 as Illinois’ first public university, Illinois State University, IllinoisState.edu is one of only 27 institutions nationwide to earn both Research 2 (R2) and Opportunity Colleges and Universities (OCU) designations by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education, which recognizes campuses that foster student success and research. We enroll approximately 21,000 students in six colleges. Our new strategic plan, Excellence by Design: 2024-2029, lists our seven core values: Excellence in Teaching, Learning, and Scholarship; Individualized Attention; Equity, Diversity, Access, and Belonging; Collaboration; Community and Civic Engagement; Respect; and Integrity. By acting on these values, we create a learning environment that results in our university being the first-choice public university in Illinois for high-achieving, motivated students who seek an individualized educational experience combined with the resources of a large university. Learn more about Illinois State’s Metrics of Excellence at IllinoisState.edu/PointsofPride . Bloomington-Normal: Illinois State University is located in the growing twin cities of Bloomington and Normal, with a metro population of approximately 172,000. The community is also home to Illinois Wesleyan University, Heartland Community College, St. Joseph Medical Center, Carle BroMenn Medical Center, COUNTRY Financial, State Farm Insurance’s International Headquarters, Central Illinois Regional Airport, and electric vehicle manufacturer Rivian Motors. The community has distinguished itself for its outstanding school systems, and its citizens’ high level of educational attainment, as well as its parks and recreation, health care, vibrant fine arts scene, job growth, economic opportunity, historic sites, and low crime rates. Bloomington made Livability’s top 100 Best Places to Live for three consecutive years, from 2024 to 2026 and Normal ranked No. 3 on College Values Online’s list of Best Small College Towns in America (2026). Bloomington-Normal is conveniently located about three hours from Indianapolis; two hours from both Chicago and St. Louis; and an hour from Peoria, Champaign-Urbana, Decatur, and Springfield. Many of these locations are accessible from Bloomington-Normal via Amtrak, which is located one block from Illinois State’s campus. For more information on our community, visit visitbn.org . Salary Rate / Pay Rate Salary is $72,828–$81,600, commensurate with qualifications and experience Required Qualifications • Ph.D. in Geology, Environmental Science, Environmental Engineering, or a closely related field, with a research focus in one or more of the areas described above; ABD candidates will be considered if the degree will be completed before the starting date • Expertise in one or more of the following areas: aqueous or low-temperature geochemistry, hydrochemistry, biogeochemistry, contaminant transport, and/or urban environmental chemistry • State law mandates demonstrable oral proficiency in the English language as a requirement of this position Work Hours Varies Proposed Starting Date August 16, 2027 Required Applicant Documents Please provide the following as separate .pdf files: • Letter of Application • Teaching Philosophy Statement (up to 2 pages) • Research Agenda (up to 2 pages) • Curriculum Vitae • Names and contact information for 3 References Please Note : These documents are required to be submitted online in order to complete the application process. Please have these documents ready prior to clicking on \"Apply\" Special Instructions for Applicants The review of applications will begin on November 2, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Sponsorship: Applicants for this position must be currently legally authorized to work for Illinois State University in the United States.  Illinois State University will not sponsor or take over the sponsorship of an employment visa for this opportunity.  Illinois State University is not a qualifying employer for the STEM OPT benefit: only the 12-month OPT may be used to work at Illinois State University. All work under this appointment is required to be performed from within the State of Illinois. Illinois State University does not authorize out-of-state work. Contact Information for Applicants Questions about the search should be directed to Eric Peterson, Department Chair ( geochemistrysearch@ilstu.edu ; 309-438-7865) Important Information for Applicants This position is subject to a criminal background investigation and if applicable, an employment history review, based on University Policy 3.1.30 and any offer of employment is contingent upon you passing a satisfactory criminal background investigation and/or an employment history review. You may not begin work until the criminal background investigation results have been received and cleared by Human Resources. Illinois State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran. If you are an individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) or other state or federal law you may request an accommodation by contacting the Office of Equal Opportunity and Access at (309) 438-3383 . The Office of Equal Opportunity and Access will hold any confidential information you provide in confidence. If you are having difficulty accessing the system, please call Human Resources at (309) 438-8311 . Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) bf5dede0 Last Name (required) db4b44dc Email (required) 68c3174c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign up for job alerts Job Alert a4f7a2ff Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type On Campus On Campus Locations Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States First Name (required) ed6168e2 Last Name (required) 68c08ca0 Email (required) 02f40fcc Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Illinois State University, Normal, IL USA Cookie Preferences Privacy Statement Appropriate Use Policy Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://jobsearch.illinoisstate.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-full-professor-of-electrical-engineering-normal-illinois-illinois-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Electrical Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Electrical Engineering - Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States Home Job Postings Applicant Accomodations Community My Profile Kiosk mode Job Description Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Electrical Engineering Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States On Campus Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Electrical Engineering Employee Classification: Asst Professor Division Name: Academic Affairs College/Unit: College of Engineering Department: Electrical Engineering Campus Location: Normal, IL Job Summary The Department of Electrical Engineering (EE Department) in the new College of Engineering (CEG) at Illinois State University (ISU) invites applications for one open rank tenure-track position beginning on August 16, 2027. An earlier start date is possible, conditional upon EE Department budget/ needs. As we continue to grow the rigor of our academic programs, we are seeking a qualified candidate with “interdisciplinary expertise” in areas closely aligned with Autonomous Systems and/or Hybrid Electric Vehicle (HEV) Systems. We highly value interdisciplinary expertise that is at the frontiers of computer engineering and electrical engineering. Valued areas of candidate expertise include but are not limited to electric vehicle (EV) battery management systems and charging technologies; intelligent vehicle sensing technologies; vehicle electronics, embedded systems, and sensors; etc. Candidates whose research/teaching expertise complements the above highly valued areas (e.g., AI/ML-enabled vehicle systems; automotive networking; autonomous/connected vehicle systems; cybersecurity; edge computing; embedded and sensing systems; Internet of things and/or vehicles; secure V2V communications, and vehicle autonomy simulation, etc.) are also encouraged to apply. Because the College is in its foundational stages, we are seeking a candidate who can adapt quickly, be flexible in terms of workload distribution, and serve as a founding member of the EE Department. Responsibilities for the position will change from year to year until the College reaches steady state by 2029-2030 or slightly thereafter. Job responsibilities will include curriculum and lab development; effective undergraduate teaching and research, first-year design and senior design project advising; grant writing and research/scholarship; ISU service, including K-12 visits, industry collaborations, and workshops for student recruitment; and external service, including societies (e.g., ACM & IEEE). Salary, Rank, and Tenure: The position is a nine-month, tenure-track appointment with the possibility of summer teaching. Salary, rank, and the status of tenure (probationary tenure-track or tenured) are commensurate with qualifications and experience. A comprehensive benefits package is included. Illinois State University Benefits Highlights: • Insurance benefits , including health, dental, vision, and life - Retirement and supplemental retirement planning options - Tuition waiver benefits available to staff as well as their eligible dependents • Paid holidays and administrative closures during Thanksgiving and Winter Break • Paid benefit time (e.g., personal plus time and sick time) Additional University Benefit information, including information regarding eligibility to participate in the State Universities Retirement System and the State of Illinois Group Insurance program, can be reviewed here: https://hr.illinoisstate.edu/benefits/ Additional Information The College of Engineering (CEG) is the newest College at ISU. We welcomed our second cohort of students in Fall 2026, and we will graduate our first cohort of students in Spring 2029. The CEG will emphasize project-based learning and applied research and demonstrate the societal impact engineers make across communities. We will be a leader in educating engineers and plan to be a leader in transforming engineering education to students coming from all backgrounds. For any additional information, please visit the CEG website ( https://illinoisstate.edu/college-engineering/ ). Illinois State University, IllinoisState.edu , was founded in 1857 as Illinois’ first public university. We enroll approximately 21,000 students in six colleges. Our new strategic plan, Excellence by Design: 2024-2029, lists our seven core values: Excellence in Teaching, Learning, and Scholarship; Individualized Attention; Equity, Diversity, Access, and Belonging; Collaboration; Community and Civic Engagement; Respect; and Integrity. By acting on these values, we create a learning environment that results in our university being the first-choice public university in Illinois for high-achieving, motivated students who seek an individualized educational experience combined with the resources of a large university. Learn more about Illinois State’s Metrics of Excellence at IllinoisState.edu/PointsofPride . Bloomington-Normal Community: ISU is located in the growing twin cities of Bloomington and Normal, with a metro population of approximately 172,000. The community is also home to Illinois Wesleyan University, Heartland Community College, St. Joseph Medical Center, Carle BroMenn Medical Center, COUNTRY Financial, State Farm Insurance’s International Headquarters, Central Illinois Regional Airport, and truck manufacturer Rivian Motors. The community has distinguished itself for its outstanding school systems, and its citizens’ high level of educational attainment, as well as its parks and recreation, health care, vibrant fine arts scene, job growth, economic opportunity, historic sites, and low crime rates. Bloomington made Livability’s top 100 Best Places to Live (2024) and ranked No. 3 on College Values Online’s list of Best Small College Towns in America (2024). Bloomington-Normal is conveniently located about three hours from Indianapolis; two hours from both Chicago and St. Louis; and an hour from Peoria, Champaign-Urbana, Decatur, and Springfield. Many of these locations are accessible from Bloomington-Normal via Amtrak, which is located one block from ISU. For more information on our community, visit https://www.visitbn.org . Salary Rate / Pay Rate Assistant Professor $80,000 – $92,500; Associate Professor $95,000 – $125,000;Full Professor $115,000 – $135,000, commensurate with qualifications and experience for each rank Required Qualifications 1) A terminal degree in Computer Engineering or Electrical Engineering or a closely related field. ABD candidates with an expected completion of a PhD by August 2027 will also be considered. 2) Research expertise on the frontiers of computer engineering and electrical engineering (i.e., autonomous and hybrid electric vehicle systems or closely related area of primary expertise); or complementary expertise (e.g., AI/ML-enabled vehicle systems, automotive networking, autonomous/connected vehicle systems, cybersecurity, embedded and sensing systems, Internet of things & vehicles, secure V2V communications, vehicle autonomy simulation, etc.). 3) Teaching expertise and/or interest in the frontiers of computer engineering and electrical engineering (i.e., autonomous and hybrid electric vehicle systems or a closely related area). 4) Experience or interest in building a computer engineering advisory track for our EE students. 5) In addition to qualifications (1) through (4), candidates must be able to demonstrate oral proficiency in the English language as a requirement for this position, as mandated by IL law. Work Hours Varies Proposed Starting Date August 16th, 2027. An earlier start date (e.g., July 2027) is possible subject to EE Department’s needs. Required Applicant Documents 1) Cover letter describing why the candidate is interested in joining a founding college (max 2 pages); 2) Research expertise/interests on the frontiers of Computer Engg. & Electrical Engg. (max 2 pages); 3) Teaching experience/philosophy and experience/vision of course/lab development (max 4 pages); 4) Curriculum vitae; 5) Name, affiliation, and contact information (email/phone) of at least three professional references. Please Note : These documents are required to be submitted online in order to complete the application process. Please have these documents ready prior to clicking on \"Apply\" Special Instructions for Applicants Review of applications will begin on January 11th, 2027, and will continue until the position is filled. Contact Information for Applicants eesearch@ilstu.edu Important Information for Applicants This position is subject to a criminal background investigation and if applicable, an employment history review, based on University Policy 3.1.30 and any offer of employment is contingent upon you passing a satisfactory criminal background investigation and/or an employment history review. You may not begin work until the criminal background investigation results have been received and cleared by Human Resources. Illinois State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran. If you are an individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) or other state or federal law you may request an accommodation by contacting the Office of Equal Opportunity and Access at (309) 438-3383 . The Office of Equal Opportunity and Access will hold any confidential information you provide in confidence. If you are having difficulty accessing the system, please call Human Resources at (309) 438-8311 . Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 1c261055 Last Name (required) 5acbd95f Email (required) 0ed0e7c4 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 81aadf14 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type On Campus On Campus Locations Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States First Name (required) 5912b298 Last Name (required) 48d94900 Email (required) 15b52975 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Illinois State University, Normal, IL USA Cookie Preferences Privacy Statement Appropriate Use Policy Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
