    "https://jobsearch.illinoisstate.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-professor-in-health-informatics-and-management-normal-illinois-illinois-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Health Informatics and Management",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Health Informatics and Management - Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States Home Job Postings Applicant Accomodations Community My Profile Kiosk mode Job Description Assistant/Associate Professor in Health Informatics and Management Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States On Campus Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant/Associate Professor in Health Informatics and Management Employee Classification: Asst Professor Division Name: Academic Affairs College/Unit: College of Applied Science and Technology Department: Health Sciences Campus Location: Normal, IL Job Summary The Department of Health Sciences (HSC) invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-track position of Assistant/Associate Professor in Health Informatics and Management in the CAHIIM-accredited Health Information Management program, titled Health Informatics and Management, beginning August 16, 2027. We seek candidates who are highly qualified and motivated to teach foundational courses in health information management and health informatics, to develop a research program, and to engage in service activities that support the department, college, university, and profession. A successful candidate will be expected to pursue cross-functional, integrative curriculum development and to incorporate a pedagogical approach that involves students in authentic experiential learning. Candidates will be expected to teach courses such as data analytics, revenue cycle management, healthcare law, healthcare quality, healthcare finance, health information systems, and other courses to support the Department of Health Sciences. Candidates will be expected to develop a focused area of research, including publication in referred journals, and provide service to the campus and professional communities. For consideration at the associate level, applicants should have an appropriate record of teaching excellence and scholarship. The position is a nine-month, tenure track appointment with the possibility of summer teaching. Salary and rank are commensurate with qualifications and experience. The locus of annual evaluation, tenure, and promotion in rank will be in the Department of Health Sciences. University Benefit Highlights: - Insurance benefits, including health, dental, vision, and life - Retirement and supplemental retirement planning options - Tuition waiver benefits available to staff as well as their eligible dependents - Paid holiday/administrative closures during Thanksgiving and Winter Breaks - Paid benefit time For more University Benefit information: https://hr.illinoisstate.edu/benefits/ Information regarding eligibility for participation in the State Universities Retirement System and the State of Illinois Group Insurance program can be reviewed here https://hr.illinoisstate.edu/benefits/insurance/. Additional Information The Department of Health Sciences (HSC) is one of six departments and two schools in the College of Applied Science and Technology (www.cast.illinoisstate.edu). There are 17 tenure and non-tenure track faculty members, a full-time academic advisor, a student success coordinator, and one civil service support staff in the department. The Department of Health Sciences has an on-line Master of Public Health (MPH) Degree that was started in Fall 2023. The Department houses the Central Illinois Area Health Education Center (AHEC). The HSC faculty and staff are committed to student-centered departmental and programmatic excellence. The Health Informatics and Management program (with approximately 80 undergraduate majors), previously titled the Medical Record Administration Program, graduated its first class in 1973. The program is committed to providing extraordinary learning opportunities that prepare graduates to be in-demand professionals in health information management and informatics settings. The Health Informatics and Management Program now has three sequences: Health Informatics , Healthcare Leadership , and RHIT to HIM . The Health Informatics and Healthcare Leadership sequences are traditional on-campus programs. The RHIT to HIM fully online program is designed for individuals who already hold the RHIT credential who want to further their education by obtaining a bachelor’s degree. All program sequences are accredited by The Commission on Accreditation for Health Informatics & Information Management Education (CAHIIM). All sequences complete a professional practice experience before graduating, with the in-person sequences completing a junior and senior year professional practice experience. Upon graduation, students in the program are eligible to take the RHIA certification exam. Illinois State University llinois State University was founded in 1857 as Illinois’ first public university. We enroll approximately 21,000 students in seven colleges. Our new strategic plan, Excellence by Design: 2024-2030, lists our seven core values: Excellence in Teaching, Learning, and Scholarship; Individualized Attention; Equity, Diversity, Access, and Belonging; Collaboration; Community and Civic Engagement; Respect; and Integrity. By acting on these values, we create a learning environment that results in our university being the first-choice public university in Illinois for high-achieving, motivated students who seek an individualized educational experience combined with the resources of a large university. Learn more about Illinois State’s Metrics of Excellence at https://strategicplan.illinoisstate.edu/metrics/ . Bloomington-Normal Community Bloomington-Normal: Illinois State University is located in the growing twin cities of Bloomington and Normal, with a metro population of approximately 172,000. The community is also home to Illinois Wesleyan University, Heartland Community College, St. Joseph Medical Center, Carle BroMenn Medical Center, COUNTRY Financial, State Farm Insurance’s International Headquarters, Central Illinois Regional Airport, and electric vehicle manufacturer Rivian Motors. The community has distinguished itself for its outstanding school systems, and its citizens’ high level of educational attainment, as well as its parks and recreation, health care, vibrant fine arts scene, job growth, economic opportunity, historic sites, and low crime rates. Bloomington made Livability’s top 100 Best Places to Live (2024) and ranked No. 3 on College Values Online’s list of Best Small College Towns in America (2024). Bloomington-Normal is conveniently located about three hours from Indianapolis; two hours from both Chicago and St. Louis; and an hour from Peoria, Champaign-Urbana, Decatur, and Springfield. Many of these locations are accessible from Bloomington-Normal via Amtrak, which is located one block from Illinois State’s campus. For more information on our community, visit visitbn.org . Salary Rate / Pay Rate Assistant Professor $75,000-$82,000 commensurate with qualifications and experience. Associate Professor $85,000-$93,000 commensurate with qualifications and experience. Required Qualifications Applicants must have at least a master’s degree plus 30 doctoral credit hours completed by May 12, 2028, with at least one degree in health information management, health informatics, or a commensurate field, and the RHIA (Registered Health Information Management Administrator) certification. Candidates must be able to demonstrate oral proficiency in the English language as a requirement for this position, as mandated by state law. Work Hours Varies Proposed Starting Date August 16, 2027 Required Applicant Documents 1) Letter of application 2) Teaching philosophy 3) Research statement 4) Curriculum vitae 5) The names and contact details of 3 references Please Note : These documents are required to be submitted online in order to complete the application process. Please have these documents ready prior to clicking on \"Apply\" Special Instructions for Applicants Review of applications will begin October 26, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Contact Information for Applicants Dr. Liangcheng Yang, lyang@ilstu.edu Important Information for Applicants This position is subject to a criminal background investigation and if applicable, an employment history review, based on University Policy 3.1.30 and any offer of employment is contingent upon you passing a satisfactory criminal background investigation and/or an employment history review. You may not begin work until the criminal background investigation results have been received and cleared by Human Resources. Illinois State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran. If you are an individual with a disability and need a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) or other state or federal law you may request an accommodation by contacting the Office of Equal Opportunity and Access at (309) 438-3383 . The Office of Equal Opportunity and Access will hold any confidential information you provide in confidence. If you are having difficulty accessing the system, please call Human Resources at (309) 438-8311 . Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 1e4db7b0 Last Name (required) 8e1993ea Email (required) 86033bcc Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 3090a1cb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type On Campus On Campus Locations Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States Normal, Illinois, Illinois, United States First Name (required) e2f1d9ae Last Name (required) 